Z||000007||Ed||03-09-2001||12:51 AM||||"Sporty" cars I've owned.  And I've enjoyed them all for different reasons.<P>1964 Pontiac GTO, four-speed, with Tri-Power (bought new in 1964) Really great in a straight line, but tiny brakes and slow steering.  I sold it after two years because it wasn't "fun enough."<P>1964 Corvair Monza (in 1966) A fun car.<P>Sprites (two: fun, but pieces of junk)<P>1984 Fiero SE (bought new in 1984, but rear-ended and totalled in 1990)<P>1987 GT (replacing the SE)<P>I've liked my Fieros, especially the GT, better than any of the above.||||reg||1
